  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the interaction with HCE-4 through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving the targeting of A704, which is subsequently engaged by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This compound is a known target of Mollicellin N, and its interaction with HCE-4 is supported by multiple evidence chains. The presence of a consistent target relationship from Mollicellin N to HCE-4, through A704 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, suggests a mechanistic link that is robust across different evidence paths. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn affects HCE-4. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Mollicellin N and HCE-4, with the proposed mechanism involving the inhibition or regulation of key metabolic or signaling pathways. The consistency of the target relationships and the absence of conflicting evidence strengthens the hypothesis that Mollicellin N exerts a functional impact on HCE-4 through these molecular interactions.",
